    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d317">

                <pb facs="0520" n="450" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg450"/>

                <head>Mr. Otterbourg to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 7.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">City of Mexico,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-08-21"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 21, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to transmit herewith a
                    representation in behalf of General O’Horan, enclosure No. 1, addressed
                    officially to the President of the republic of Mexico, and presented personally
                    by me, accompanied by General Porfirio Diaz.</p>
                <p>The motives for ray intercession are fully explained in that representation, to
                    which, as will be seen by a copy of the reply, enclosure No. 2, the President
                    did not find himself at liberty to accede. I trust that the department, on
                    reference to former despatches mentioning General O’Horan’s good offices
                    exercised to the advantage of Americans, will approve of my course in this
                    instance.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>MARCUS OTTERBOURG.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
                <postscript>
                    <p>P. S.—General O’Horan was executed this morning at 6 o’clock.</p>
                    <p rendition="#right">M. O.</p>
                </postscript>



